{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792268646,"nonce":"H4bG1pkwLM59zUYFeqT/vsIQeKw=","title":"An isolated conformance case at --jit-threshold 1 occasionally ends with exit 0 and no output","message":"Seen on 2026-10-17 on macOS arm64. Running the unit suite with 'scripts/haxe_conformance.py --suites unit --modes hybrid --isolate --isolate-jobs 3' and ash --jit-threshold 1 (a wrapper that adds the flag), about one run in six reports one or two cases as CRASH or FAIL while every other run is 1069/1069. The cases differ each time (Issue10641 and Issue8959 on one run of main 70305249's binary; TestExceptions and Issue7286 on one run of a branch build; one unnamed case on an earlier run), they die within 90-150 ms, and the harness stored no detail for them.\n\nEvidence on the shape: the empty detail means the process exited 0 and printed no utest tally (a signal or a crash report would have been recorded), so this is a silent early exit, not a segfault. It does not reproduce on demand: six sweeps of all 1195 cases at threshold 1 on main's binary (7170 case runs, 3 at a time) produced no bad run, and 3 further harness runs of the same binary were clean after the one that failed.\n\nNot established: whether the exit is in ash (startup, threshold-1 eager compile) or in the environment (the harness runs three processes at once and ash stages libhl beside the program on first use). scripts/haxe_conformance.py now records 'exit 0 without a tally; last line: ...' for such a case, so the next occurrence says what the process printed; next step is to catch one with that and ASH_TIER_LOG=1.","files":null}]}